    {
      "id": "LL_WWDG_SetWindow",
      "name": "LL_WWDG_SetWindow",
      "peripheral": "WWDG",
      "library": "ll",
      "sectionId": "WWDG@ll#sec1",
      "prototype": "void LL_WWDG_SetWindow(WWDG_TypeDef * WWDGx, uint32_t Window);",
      "returnType": "void",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "WWDGx",
          "type": "WWDG_TypeDef *",
          "descEn": "WWDG Instance",
          "descZh": "窗口看门狗实例指针（F1 上固定是 WWDG）。"
        },
        {
          "name": "Window",
          "type": "uint32_t",
          "descEn": "0x00..0x7F (7 bit Window value)",
          "descZh": ""
        }
      ],
      "returnDescEn": "None",
      "returnDescZh": "",
      "briefEn": "Set the Watchdog Window value to be compared to the downcounter (7-bits W[6:0]).",
      "briefZh": "设置窗口值。喂狗时计数值必须小于该值，否则视为喂得太早并复位。",
      "usageZh": "",
      "prerequisites": [],
      "registers": [
        "WWDGx_CFR"
      ],
      "relatedFunctions": [],
      "remarks": [
        "This window value defines when write in the WWDG_CR register to program Watchdog counter is allowed. Watchdog counter value update must occur only when the counter value is lower than the Watchdog window register value. Otherwise, a MCU reset is generated if the 7-bit Watchdog counter value (in the control register) is refreshed before the downcounter has reached the watchdog window register value. Physically is possible to set the Window lower then 0x40 but it is not recommended. To generate an immediate reset, it is possible to set the Counter lower than 0x40."
      ],
      "notesZh": [],
      "exampleCode": "",
      "exampleLanguage": "c",
      "symbolRefs": [],
      "headerLine": 215,
      "definedIn": "stm32f1xx_ll_wwdg.h",
      "sourceLine": 0,
      "flags": {
        "deprecated": false,
        "isrSafe": false,
        "inline": true,
        "macroLike": false
      },
